\":0,\"year\":2025,\"type\":\"tv\",\"_score\":0.4065217391304348,\"_genreOverlap\":1}],\"seasonNumber\":6,\"seasonName\":\"Season 6\",\"seasonOverview\":\"\",\"seasonPoster\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/pE0ToeQbYpMChYGmB6gEhuJq61H.jpg\",\"seasonAirDate\":\"2019-03-11\",\"episodes\":[{\"number\":1,\"name\":\"Episode 1\",\"overview\":\"At Witley Recycling Centre in Surrey, Sarah Moore is on the lookout for three items she can salvage, spruce up and sell on for a profit.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/tgb1fwQ5AScUu4Nfth4quFWumZu.jpg\",\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2019-03-11\",\"runtime\":44},{\"number\":2,\"name\":\"Episode 2\",\"overview\":\"Upcycler Jay Blades is at Altrincham recycling centre on a mission to rescue and revive unwanted items.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/vbNvVZLiD3epNbR8OzCEFvTIYIc.jpg\",\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2019-03-12\",\"runtime\":44},{\"number\":3,\"name\":\"Episode 3\",\"overview\":\"Sarah Moore is in Surrey, checking out the cast-offs at Witley recycling centre. She and her team of artisans try to revive a 1950s TV, an art deco chair and a drum kit.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/jZAmLLV9FKjtF5bQJfStehqxLom.jpg\",\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2019-03-13\",\"runtime\":44},{\"number\":4,\"name\":\"Episode 4\",\"overview\":\"Upcycling expert EJ Osborne is scouring the skips at Woking recycling centre, searching for three items that he can rework to reveal their true potential.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/4cdtK8RhnGUbaRM4Hsv2l7yHAz5.jpg\",\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2019-03-14\",\"runtime\":44},{\"number\":5,\"name\":\"Episode 5\",\"overview\":\"Sarah Moore is scouring the recycling centre in Witley for unwanted items that she can breathe new life into.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/zOg74cA2TpICKTeQcprdZVwS1vz.jpg\",\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2019-03-15\",\"runtime\":44},{\"number\":6,\"name\":\"Episode 6\",\"overview\":\"At Witley recycling centre, upcycler extraordinaire Sarah Moore is on the lookout for three unloved items that she can save and sell on for a profit.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/44pyLw0bzhA2KDjybXCFQAT2nh1.jpg\",\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2019-03-18\",\"runtime\":44},{\"number\":7,\"name\":\"Episode 7\",\"overview\":\"In Bradford, Jay Blades is rooting around the car boots for hidden gems he can revamp. Among the items he finds are an old typewriter and a sewing machine.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/jidf7qwsIRAhDCBQfo1dpxni7iW.jpg\",\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2019-03-19\",\"runtime\":44},{\"number\":8,\"name\":\"Episode 8\",\"overview\":\"In Witley, Sarah Moore salvages some copper pipes, a Sussex armchair and two tables. But will her revamps return a profit?\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/3taJipK8aYJiKpPiGgegtUYMOuC.jpg\",\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2019-03-20\",\"runtime\":44},{\"number\":9,\"name\":\"Episode 9\",\"overview\":\"Upcycling entrepreneur EJ Osborne is at the Llanfoist recycling centre in Wales where he's on a hunt for potential loot.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/4cdtK8RhnGUbaRM4Hsv2l7yHAz5.jpg\",\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2019-03-21\",\"runtime\":44},{\"number\":10,\"name\":\"Episode 10\",\"overview\":\"In Witley, Sarah Moore salvages an old mower, two teak chairs and some Persian rugs, but will her eclectic items prove to be too past-it to make a profit?\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/8lzE0xpyQDICgyEkhVMrpnQTyoc.jpg\",\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2019-03-22\",\"runtime\":44},{\"number\":11,\"name\":\"Episode 11\",\"overview\":\"Sarah Moore is on a mission to rescue three unloved and unwanted items from Wallyford Recycling Centre in Scotland. To help her on her quest, Sarah turns to designer maker Rupert Blanchard to come up with a creative new use for some wooden garden chairs while carpenter Bruce Faulseit is tasked with turning a redundant sewing machine stand into something special. Sarah takes on the ambitious project of restyling a pair of bedside tables - but will all her hard work pay off?\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/7BzPHQd7DICjbEaWglAZTG5rF8m.jpg\",\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2019-03-25\",\"runtime\":44},{\"number\":12,\"name\":\"Episode 12\",\"overview\":\"In Altrincham in Greater Manchester, Jay Blades is scouring the recycling centre in search of three unwanted items to save and sell on. Designer-maker Ollie Allen takes on the challenge of transforming some metal springs while upholsterer Leigh-Anne Treadwell gets to work giving a new lease of life to an old blanket box. For his own project, Jay has two tables to add some creativity to, but will he succeed in finding new homes for all his upcycled items?\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/1WUbf9A1wY8orVn2SzznJYiTMN6.jpg\",\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2019-03-26\",\"runtime\":44},{\"number\":13,\"name\":\"Episode 13\",\"overview\":\"At Wallyford Recycling Centre in Scotland, upcycler extraordinaire Sarah Moore is on the lookout for three unloved items that she can save from the skip. Woodworking duo Josh and Oli get busy with a collection of wooden lawn bowls and designer Daniel Heath has the challenge of putting his stamp on a broken dining table. For her own project, Sarah has three fabric chairs to transform, but will she succeed in making all three upcycled items saleable?\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/8685UloetRIjt2eGvZWktONEXGa.jpg\",\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2019-03-27\",\"runtime\":44},{\"number\":14,\"name\":\"Episode 14\",\"overview\":\"At Midland Road Recycling Centre in Bradford, Jay Blades is sifting through the unwanted items in search of three hidden gems that he can take, transform and turn a profit on. Metalwork maestro Kev Paxton has his hands full with a collection of scaffolding poles and upholsterer Simion Hawtin-Smith has a tired rocking chair to inject some new life into. Jay sees profit-making potential in a pair of dining chairs, but will he succeed in finding new homes for all three items?\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/fO3EtW8hYSPQDFrpZtCI213300c.jpg\",\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2019-03-28\",\"runtime\":44},{\"number\":15,\"name\":\"Episode 15\",\"overview\":\"At the recycling centre in Woking, upcycling aficionado EJ Osborne unearths three hidden gems with profit-making potential. To transform his trash, EJ calls on robot maker Mark Haig to find a new use for an unwanted tape player while designer maker Rupert Blanchard has the tall order of making half a chest of drawers whole again. A draughting chair is given the upcycling treatment by EJ, but will the transformations ensure he can return a profit to the items' unsuspecting owners?\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/gikUSzR9lubnjBPPnN1yRnQg74f.jpg\",\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2019-03-29\",\"runtime\":44},{\"number\":16,\"name\":\"Episode 16\",\"overview\":\"Sarah Moore salvages three items from Wallyford recycling centre in Scotland, including a cable drum and a pair of stone statues.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/7ygP31bJKaCZYhfBchecTa8H6W7.jpg\",\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2019-04-01\",\"runtime\":44},{\"number\":17,\"name\":\"Episode 17\",\"overview\":\"EJ Osborne salvages three items from the skips at Woking recycling centre, including a dresser and a set of stepladders.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/ePiTz89wUadJ854UkGTQzEbUdM9.jpg\",\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2019-04-02\",\"runtime\":44},{\"number\":18,\"name\":\"Episode 18\",\"overview\":\"In Witley, Sarah Moore salvages an old mower, two teak chairs and some Persian rugs, but will her eclectic items prove to be too past-it to make a profit?\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/7rY734rlm8F74bm4yY5fFISPk0K.jpg\",\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2019-04-03\",\"runtime\":44},{\"number\":19,\"name\":\"Episode 19\",\"overview\":\"Sarah Moore salvages a kitchen cabinet, a wooden stool and a collection of cutlery from the skips at Witley recycling centre.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/11GbgoD0LkXZbyIjk78eF3vMPny.jpg\",\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2019-04-04\",\"runtime\":44},{\"number\":20,\"name\":\"Episode 20\",\"overview\":\"Upcycling expert EJ Osborne salvages a chest of drawers and a collection of glass jars from Llanfoist recycling centre in Wales.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/r86AI6XkM6xpMiqQQ8SotZeDwrp.jpg\",\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2019-04-05\",\"runtime\":44}],\"firstAirDate\":\"2015-09-07\"}","status":200,"url":""},"revalidate":86400,"tags":[]}